# Target C-II — conditional support-six elimination improves the one-anchor corank floor

**Date:** 2026-09-18  
**Status:** proved conditional candidate; theorem-state authority unchanged  
**Scope:** the one-anchor transpose-kernel reduction, assuming the remaining collapsed support-six endpoint is globally excluded  
**Depends on:** `target_c_free_terminal_one_anchor_corank_2026-09-18.md`; the audited support-five equality exclusion; `target_c_support6_noncollapsed_h5_h6_exclusion_2026-09-18.md`  
**Certificate:** `research/verify_target_c_free_terminal_support6_conditional_corank_2026_09_18.py`  
**Classification:** conditional propagation, not a promotion; C-II remains open

The completed noncollapsed support-six theorem changes the exact next endpoint of the
one-anchor transpose-kernel program. If the collapsed support-six branch is also
excluded by a genuinely global theorem, then the degree-pure component-size argument
starts at seven rather than six. The resulting finite coefficient and terminal
consequence are

\[
\boxed{\sigma_C\le 2n_0+n_2+{n_1\over7}}\tag{SC.1}
\]

and, with

\[
E_U=a_F+{x_A\over2}+{n_0+n_2\over2},\qquad f=a_F+n_0+n_1+n_2,
\]

\[
\boxed{\sigma_C\le {f\over7}+{26\over7}E_U.}\tag{SC.2}
\]

In the current terminal window `t_D <= mu_*+0.00710+o(1)`, the existing ledger gives
`limsup f/D <= 0.7791330455`. Hence a sequence at the pair-shield counting floor
(`E_U=o(D)`) would satisfy

\[
\boxed{\limsup {\sigma_C\over D}<0.111304721.}\tag{SC.3}
\]

This is a conditional consequence only. The certified local collapsed realization
shows why the hypothesis cannot be replaced by the local pentagon closure conditions.

## 1. Exact component-size propagation

The one-anchor theorem gives a nonzero relation component dimension at most one and
shows that every such component has at least five vertices. The support-five equality
block is excluded by the earlier reciprocal theorem. The present combined theorem
excludes every noncollapsed degree-pure support-six reciprocal block: H5 is ruled out
by the strict source-gap angle lemma, and H6 by the exact sign/order certificate.

Thus, under the additional hypothesis that the collapsed support-six endpoint has no
global realization in the canonical residual system, the next degree-pure component
size is at least seven. Each live component still contributes at most one scalar fiber
dimension, so its contribution is bounded by `n_1/7`.

The qualification “degree-pure” is binding: this note does not silently classify
arbitrary six-vertex relation graphs with extra nonparallel links.

## 2. Exact coefficient algebra

The comparison with the structural excess is the exact identity

\[
\left({f\over7}+{26\over7}E_U\right)
 -\left(2n_0+n_2+{n_1\over7}\right)
={27a_F+13x_A+7n_2\over7}\ge0.
\tag{SC.4}
\]

No asymptotic estimate or KKT multiplier lower bound is used.

## 3. Terminal propagation

The already audited terminal ledger has

\[
{f\over D}\le {M_*\over5}+2(0.00710)+o(1),\qquad
M_*=4\sqrt{\frac{\pi}{2\sqrt3}}+2(0.007707).
\]

The exact rational enclosure in the companion verifier gives

\[
{1\over7}\left({M_*\over5}+2(0.00710)\right)<0.111304721.
\]

Combining this with (SC.2) proves (SC.3) whenever `E_U=o(D)`.

## 4. C-II consequence and live obstruction

The result does not improve the canonical theorem state, because the collapsed
support-six branch is not globally excluded. It identifies the exact payoff of the
remaining global task: excluding that one branch upgrades the low-flex endpoint from
the current `n_1/6` route to `n_1/7` and lowers the pair-floor pure-contact corank
density below `0.111304721`.

The next required theorem must therefore either establish global train-corridor/source
compatibility failure for the collapsed two-parameter family or use the actual diameter
and KKT system to exclude it. The local contraction certificate is a binding regression
against any argument using only the six pentagon closures and their local turn gaps.

**Disposition:** conditional proved candidate; no theorem-state change.
